{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>לתאוה</b> — [in manuscripts] A-B [read:] two joined [letters]. The lamed of לתאוה is like בעבור." "<b>נפרד</b> — the wandering and roaming one, separated from his place to seek wisdom, on account of the desire that he desires to learn, and among all men of wisdom he will mingle and go with them."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The note 'שנים דבקים' appears to refer to a textual variant where two letters are joined; the exact meaning is uncertain and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:26.411157729Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}